              <li>Y-axis: Relative number of electrons (peak height)</li>
              <li><strong>Higher binding energy</strong> = electrons closer to nucleus = harder to remove</li>
              <li>Number of peaks = number of occupied subshells</li>
              <li>Peak height ratios match electron counts (e.g., 2:2:6 for Ne)</li>
