            <ul style="font-size:0.88em; line-height:1.7;">
              <li><strong>Coffee-cup calorimeter:</strong> Constant pressure &rarr; measures &Delta;H directly</li>
              <li><strong>Bomb calorimeter:</strong> Constant volume &rarr; measures &Delta;E (internal energy)</li>
              <li><strong>Specific heat of water:</strong> 4.184 J/(g&middot;&deg;C) — memorize this!</li>
            </ul>
            <h4 style="color:var(--gold); margin-top:12px;">Common AP Exam Pitfalls</h4>
            <ul style="font-size:0.88em; line-height:1.7; color:#ff9;">
              <li>&Delta;T = T<sub>final</sub> &minus; T<sub>initial</sub> (can be negative for cooling)</li>
              <li>If the solution temperature RISES, the reaction is exothermic (&Delta;H &lt; 0)</li>
              <li>Don't forget to convert kJ &harr; J when needed</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
