          <li><strong>Read the spontaneity verdict:</strong> ΔG < 0 means spontaneous, ΔG > 0 means non-spontaneous, ΔG = 0 means equilibrium.</li>
          <li><strong>Look at the graph</strong> showing ΔG vs. T — the line crosses zero at the crossover temperature.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Try this:</strong> Set ΔH = +100 kJ and ΔS = +200 J/K. At low T, ΔG is positive (non-spontaneous). Slide temperature up past 500 K — ΔG becomes negative! The crossover temperature is T = ΔH/ΔS = 100,000/200 = 500 K.</p>
        <p><strong>AP Tip:</strong> Watch your units! ΔH is typically in kJ but ΔS is in J/K. You must convert before using ΔG = ΔH − TΔS. When ΔH and ΔS have the same sign, spontaneity depends on temperature.</p>
